00:12:17,694 --> 00:12:20,656
-Three singles? Real moneybags, huh?
-Mmm-hmm.

238
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:26,662
I love that you carry this in your wallet.

239
00:12:26,745 --> 00:12:29,791
[chuckles] I don't know.
They could make a comeback, right?

240
00:12:29,874 --> 00:12:32,251
In high school,
it was my dream to work there,

241
00:12:32,334 --> 00:12:34,045
but I was too intimidated to apply

242
00:12:34,128 --> 00:12:36,923
because all the cool older kids
from school worked there.

243
00:12:37,006 --> 00:12:39,133
Mmm. You weren't a cool kid?

244
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:42,845
I find that hard to believe.

245
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:45,639
In high school,
you would have totally intimidated me.

246
00:12:45,722 --> 00:12:47,433
-No!
-Yeah. No doubt.

247
00:12:47,516 --> 00:12:50,144
I was so nice to the losers.

248
00:12:50,227 --> 00:12:52,521
[chuckles] Hmm. Uh-huh.

249
00:12:54,315 --> 00:12:57,819
You know, I wasn't that big
of a loser in high school.

250
00:12:59,236 --> 00:13:02,865
Don't want to brag,
but I was homecoming king.

251
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:07,286
-Really?
-Mmm-hmm.

252
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:09,872
I mean, it was a class size
of, like, 40 people,

253
00:13:09,955 --> 00:13:12,541
so I didn't have to impress
too many folks, but... 

254
00:13:13,042 --> 00:13:14,752
yeah, I was homecoming king.

255
00:13:15,795 --> 00:13:18,255
-[helicopter hovering]
-[sirens wailing in the distance]

256
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:19,924
-I should go.
-[keys jangle]

257
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:22,134
Okay. Yeah.

258
00:13:24,303 --> 00:13:28,933
-I'll, uh... see you around.
-All right. Yeah. Whatever.

259
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:31,685
-[sirens wailing]
-What is going on?

260
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,814
What the fuck is that?

261
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,866
[indistinct chatter]

262
00:13:46,742 --> 00:13:50,496
Holy shit.

263
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:53,415
Maybe we should go inside.

264
00:13:53,499 --> 00:13:56,460
It feels, like, a little dangerous
to be out here. You know what I mean?

265
00:13:56,543 --> 00:13:58,670
-[yells and laughs]
-[shrieks] Jeez, Chris!

266
00:13:58,754 --> 00:14:01,507
-[grunts] I got you good, man!
-You scared me.

267
00:14:01,590 --> 00:14:03,425
Whoo. You scared me there.

268
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:05,052
-Ah, I had to do that, man.
-Ah.

269
00:14:06,012 --> 00:14:07,304
Oh, hey, Mickey, right?

270
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:08,639
-Hey.
-Yeah. Hey.

271
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:10,141
Mickey, you remember Chris, yeah?

272
00:14:10,224 --> 00:14:14,103
Totally. Yeah, we met the night
I couldn't rhyme Carlito's Way.

273
00:14:14,186 --> 00:14:17,398
[laughing] Oh, that's right.
That's a tough word, though.

274
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:19,483
-It is. It's very tough. Yeah.
-Yeah.

275
00:14:19,566 --> 00:14:21,110
Whoo! How crazy is this, huh?

276
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:22,236
Yeah.

277
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:23,988
Whoa! God, man,

278
00:14:24,071 --> 00:14:26,115
I feel like I'm in a video game right now.

279
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:27,241
-Yes.
-Yeah.

280
00:14:27,324 --> 00:14:30,578
-Exactly. This is, like, unreal right now.
-God, it's so weird...

281
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:33,080
-What are you two doing?
-Oh, we're just hanging out.

282
00:14:33,164 --> 00:14:35,124
-Oh.
-I gotta get home.

283
00:14:35,207 --> 00:14:37,376
Okay, folks, you need to go
back inside immediately.

284
00:14:37,459 --> 00:14:38,669
[Mickey] Oh, shit.

285
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:41,505
Um, Officer, sorry, uh,

286
00:14:41,588 --> 00:14:43,799
I don't live here,
so could I just go to my car

287
00:14:43,882 --> 00:14:47,011
and I'll just get out of here.
One less person you have to worry about.

288
00:14:47,094 --> 00:14:49,471
Springwood is on lockdown.
Nobody can leave until further notice.

289
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:52,849
But see, the thing is,
I've got some extenuating circumstances

290
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:54,894
that necessitate me leaving now.

291
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:56,938
What part of "go inside"
don't you understand?

292
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:59,106
Go inside now. We'll let you know
when it's safe to leave.

293
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:00,649
Fine. Whatever.

294
00:15:00,732 --> 00:15:03,652
Ugh. What a d-bag.

295
00:15:03,735 --> 00:15:05,487
Hey, Frank, Allan. What's up?

296
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:08,574
Check out the cop cars.
Looks like my ride's here.

297
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:10,159
[both laughing]

298
00:15:11,743 --> 00:15:13,245
That's funny. That's good.

299
00:15:13,329 --> 00:15:14,914
Hey, what the hell's going on here?
You guys know?

300
00:15:14,997 --> 00:15:16,373
-You guys don't know?
-Unh-unh.

301
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,000
There was a car chase on the freeway

302
00:15:18,084 --> 00:15:20,002
that made its way here
into the Springwood.

303
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:22,838
Then the wacko crashes his car
into the rec center

304
00:15:22,921 --> 00:15:24,590
-and takes off running.
-Oh, my God.

305
00:15:24,673 --> 00:15:27,509
And now the cops, they're searching
the grounds, trying to catch this guy.

306
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:30,387
-Wow. What are they after him for?
-Drug trafficking.

307
00:15:30,471 --> 00:15:32,056
Really? You know that for sure?

308
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:35,309
No. But I guarantee you
it's drug trafficking.

309
00:15:35,392 --> 00:15:38,104
That's why he ran.
That's what drug traffickers do. They run.

310
00:15:38,187 --> 00:15:40,647
Or maybe he robbed a convenience store
and he's on the run?

311
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:43,067
Maybe he's got a bunch
of parking tickets he hasn't paid for.

312
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:44,193
Could be a serial killer.

313
00:15:44,276 --> 00:15:45,777
-I like that.
-Mmm-hmm.

314
00:15:45,861 --> 00:15:47,446
'Cause he's worried if he gets caught,

315
00:15:47,529 --> 00:15:49,949
they'll be able to tie him
to all his unsolved murders.

316
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:51,867
And who's, uh, Inspector Poirot here?

317
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:54,495
Oh, this is Mickey. Mickey, Frank, Allan.

318
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:58,832
Allan, Frank, Mickey.
Do you guys wanna go inside?

319
00:15:58,915 --> 00:16:00,251
You know what? Come to our place.

320
00:16:00,334 --> 00:16:02,419
-Come on.
-It's safer if we stick together.

321
00:16:02,503 --> 00:16:04,046
[Chris] If we don't stick together,
we die.

322
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:05,297
-No, we don't.
-[chuckles]

323
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,799
I don't know all the facts,
but come on, let's hang out.

324
00:16:07,883 --> 00:16:08,884
Come on. Let's go.

325
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:12,804
-Is this cool?
-Yeah, I mean, safety in numbers.

326
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:16,475
Oh, I call massage chair.

327
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:19,270
Hey, the secret of that thing
is to use the neck roller

328
00:16:19,353 --> 00:16:21,313
and the vibration mode at the same time.

329
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:23,983
Hey, whoa, whoa,
would you be easy on it, though, right?

330
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:26,568
I got a date next week,
and it needs to be functional.

331
00:16:26,652 --> 00:16:28,945
-[chuckles]
-Guys, I like this place.

332
00:16:29,030 --> 00:16:30,947
-Very, very cool.
-Thank you.

333
00:16:31,032 --> 00:16:32,158
Why's yours different than Gus'?

334
00:16:32,241 --> 00:16:34,410
I thought all these places
were supposed to be the same.

335
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:37,079
This is how it was when we first moved in.

336
00:16:37,163 --> 00:16:39,498
Management wanted to redecorate
a couple of years ago,

337
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:41,208
-but we liked it like it was.
-That's right.

338
00:16:41,292 --> 00:16:43,544
This is our place
and no one's gonna tell us to change it.

339
00:16:43,627 --> 00:16:45,171
Yeah, plus, give it a couple of years.

340
00:16:45,254 --> 00:16:48,049
Southwestern decor
is gonna make a big comeback.

341
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:49,925
You know, that's true.
I just read an article.

342
00:16:50,008 --> 00:16:53,345
Every 20 years, trends recycle.

343
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:55,389
How long do these lockdowns usually last?

344
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:57,641
Ugh, I don't know. Ten hours?

345
00:16:57,724 --> 00:16:59,101
-Give or take.
-Yeah.

346
00:16:59,185 --> 00:17:00,769
-Shit. Really?
-Yeah.

347
00:17:00,852 --> 00:17:02,146
Once there was a lockdown

348
00:17:02,229 --> 00:17:04,690
because Allan forgot his duffel bag
at the rec center

349
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:10,696
-and they thought it was a bomb.
-Oh, ridiculous. It was October 2001.

350
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:13,031
So everyone's living in a culture of fear.

351
00:17:13,115 --> 00:17:14,658
Oh, I remember those days, man.

352
00:17:14,741 --> 00:17:18,120
[exhales sharply] Before that,
you could bring a box cutter on a plane,

353
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:20,289
but then after, it was a whole thing.

354
00:17:22,083 --> 00:17:23,167
Hey, Mickey, I'm sorry.

355
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:25,752
I feel like I forced you to come out here
and now you're stuck.

356
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:27,963
It's fine, dude.
You didn't force me to do anything.

357
00:17:28,047 --> 00:17:31,300
Hey. Let's take this conversation
to the conversation pit.

358
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:34,136
-Hey, look at that now.
-Oh, you guys have a telescope.

359
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:37,598
Maybe I could, like,
see a way to my car from here.

360
00:17:37,681 --> 00:17:40,184
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
Be careful with that, little girl.

361
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:42,436
You're gonna mess up my equatorial mount.

362
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:43,979
[Chris] God, this is, like, so fun.

363
00:17:44,062 --> 00:17:45,939
I'm only seeing buildings,
buildings, buildings.

364
00:17:46,022 --> 00:17:47,483
What are you looking for?

365
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:50,277
I'm looking for my car.
I'm trying to find a way to my car.

366
00:17:50,361 --> 00:17:51,820
What parking lot are you in?
Do you remember?

367
00:17:51,903 --> 00:17:53,780
I think E. Does that make sense?

368
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:54,948
-It does.
-Okay.

369
00:17:55,031 --> 00:17:56,825
-Can you see E--
-You cannot see E from here.

370
00:17:56,908 --> 00:17:59,035
You can see pretty much
the other parts of the complex.

371
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:00,287
What do you wanna do? Get out?

372
00:18:00,371 --> 00:18:01,622
-Yeah.
-I can get you out of here.

373
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:05,459
Hey, so what's, uh...
What's going on over here, dude?

374
00:18:05,542 --> 00:18:07,211
-With, like, Mickey? Or...
-Yeah.

375
00:18:07,294 --> 00:18:10,297
-You guys, like, hooking up?
-No. No.

376
00:18:10,381 --> 00:18:15,219
Actually we're in a bit of a Meryl Streep,
Alec Baldwin situation right now.

377
00:18:16,137 --> 00:18:17,763
-Huh?
-It's complicated.

378
00:18:17,846 --> 00:18:19,348
-[chuckles] Oh.
-Oh.

379
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:20,641
Very nice.

380
00:18:20,724 --> 00:18:21,808
-Yeah.
-[all chuckle]

381
00:18:21,892 --> 00:18:24,936
Well, it's not great but, uh...
Yeah, I don't know.

382
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:29,400
I mean, for a number of reasons
we're actually trying not to hook up,

383
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:32,611
so this lockdown is not helping things.

384
00:18:32,694 --> 00:18:35,071
Oh. Got ya.

385
00:18:35,156 --> 00:18:36,948
-The temptation here--
-Yeah.

386
00:18:37,032 --> 00:18:38,742
There's a lot of excitement in the air.

387
00:18:38,825 --> 00:18:40,827
A lot of tension. Like, you can feel it.

388
00:18:40,911 --> 00:18:43,205
-Yeah. Yeah.
-It's, like, electric. Yeah.

389
00:18:43,289 --> 00:18:44,956
Think about all the people
who are fucking tonight.

390
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:47,168
-Yeah.
-Like, nine months from now,

391
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:51,129
there's gonna be all these Springwood
lockdown babies running around.

392
00:18:51,213 --> 00:18:53,132
Hey, guys, what if we took this up
on the roof?

393
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:55,467
And maybe I could find,
like, a route to my car.

394
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:57,803
Yeah, sure, I like that idea.
What do you think?

395
00:18:57,886 --> 00:18:59,054
-Yeah.
-Hey.

396
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:00,931
I'm gonna get the BB guns for safety.

397
00:19:01,014 --> 00:19:03,099
-They're in the hobby closet.
-I know.

398
00:19:03,184 --> 00:19:04,601
Yeah, that's smart thinking.

399
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:07,062
I mean, as long as the cops
don't think we're some sniper

400
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,814
and try to take us out or anything. Right?

401
00:19:08,897 --> 00:19:10,941
Sounds like this night's
just getting started.

402
00:19:11,858 --> 00:19:14,361
-[helicopter hovering]
-[indistinct chatter]

403
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:19,408
Uh, look it, boxes of wine and condoms.

404
00:19:19,491 --> 00:19:21,660
[Gus] Wow, somebody had
a real party up here.

405
00:19:21,743 --> 00:19:24,205
Ugh, you know what, Gus? Forget my car.

406
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:26,373
-Yeah?
-It's hopeless. I've just...

407
00:19:26,457 --> 00:19:28,875
My only shot
is to get over the property line

408
00:19:28,959 --> 00:19:30,752
and then call for an Uber.

409
00:19:30,836 --> 00:19:34,756
Okay. Well, yeah, I mean, if you think
that'd work, you should go for it.

410
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:38,635
-I think if I can get to that fence...
-Uh-huh.

411
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:40,136
-and scale it...
-Yeah.

412
00:19:40,221 --> 00:19:42,848
and just run through those trees...

413
00:19:42,931 --> 00:19:44,140
No, I can see that. Yes.

414
00:19:44,225 --> 00:19:45,351
-[Mickey sighs]
-Yeah.

415
00:19:46,393 --> 00:19:50,314
-Why? What are you thinking? What's wrong?
-All right. I just... I need a smoke.

416
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:52,733
-I need a smoke.
-Okay.

417
00:19:54,318 --> 00:19:55,569
[indistinct chatter]

418
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:01,658
[Chris] All I can see is a tree.
Let me adjust this.

419
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:05,078
[Frank stutters] No, I told you,
I'll do the adjusting. Come on.

420
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:09,541
-You need help with that?
-Yeah.

421
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,090
There you go.

422
00:20:19,175 --> 00:20:21,762
-I should get out of here.
-Yeah.

423
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:25,474
You sure, with this fucking maniac
running around here?

424
00:20:25,557 --> 00:20:28,727
Yeah. 'Cause if I stay,
you know, it's gonna be...

425
00:20:30,061 --> 00:20:33,106
Right. Yeah, yeah, yeah.
No, no, no. I get it.

426
00:20:34,691 --> 00:20:37,319
Well, can I go with you?
I think I'd feel a lot better

427
00:20:37,403 --> 00:20:40,864
if I could just get you to the road,
to the Uber and stuff.

428
00:20:40,947 --> 00:20:43,575
Like a... covert mission.

429
00:20:43,659 --> 00:20:44,951
-Right.
-Yeah.

430
00:20:45,035 --> 00:20:47,329
Like a total covert mission situation.

431
00:20:47,413 --> 00:20:49,039
-That's cool.
-Okay.

432
00:20:49,122 --> 00:20:50,374
-Yeah. Hey!
-Let's do it.

433
00:20:50,457 --> 00:20:52,334
Guys, I'm gonna make a run for it.

434
00:20:52,418 --> 00:20:54,503
Yeah. I'm gonna help Mickey
with her great escape.

435
00:20:54,586 --> 00:20:57,381
I'll tell you what,
take the BB gun for protection.

436
00:20:57,881 --> 00:20:59,341
-Oh...
-Mmm, no, thank you.

437
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:01,009
-That's all right.
-Then take the flashlight.

438
00:21:01,092 --> 00:21:02,511
But if you do this,
you got to do it right.

439
00:21:02,594 --> 00:21:04,054
-If you hold it from the front...
-Uh-huh.

440
00:21:04,137 --> 00:21:05,347
it's not only a flashlight.

441
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:08,099
Bam! It becomes a billy club. Bow. Boom.

442
00:21:08,183 --> 00:21:09,726
-Whoa. Uh...
-No, thank you.

443
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:12,062
I think that'll do more harm than good,
but thank you.

444
00:21:12,145 --> 00:21:13,939
-All right. Appreciate it.
-Thanks. Bye, guys.

445
00:21:14,981 --> 00:21:16,775
-Take no prisoners. Okay?
-All right.

446
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:19,820
God, it's nights like this
I wish I had a remote-control drone.

447
00:21:20,987 --> 00:21:22,072
[indistinct chatter]

448
00:21:23,324 --> 00:21:24,700
-Are we clear?
-Yeah.

449
00:21:29,621 --> 00:21:31,248
[Mickey] Go to the left. Go to the left.

450
00:21:32,165 --> 00:21:33,917
[indistinct radio chatter]

451
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:38,839
Hey, what the fuck are you two doing
down there? Are you crazy?

452
00:21:38,922 --> 00:21:41,550
[shushes] Please, can you just be quiet?
We're just--

453
00:21:41,633 --> 00:21:43,594
You're gonna get yourselves killed!

454
00:21:43,677 --> 00:21:45,303
Is this what you fucking do?

455
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:47,723
You just come out on your balcony
and yell at people all night?

456
00:21:47,806 --> 00:21:49,140
Is that... That's your fun?

457
00:21:49,224 --> 00:21:52,519
I fucking have a full, rich life,
all right? This is part of it.

458
00:21:52,603 --> 00:21:54,187
Great. I don't have time for this.
We gotta go.

459
00:21:54,270 --> 00:21:56,773
You assholes! You're gonna get killed!

460
00:21:56,857 --> 00:21:58,442
[indistinct chatter]

461
00:22:03,238 --> 00:22:06,032
-Oh, man, this is kind of cool.
-Yeah!

462
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:08,452
-It's got my blood pumping, you know?
-Totally!

463
00:22:08,535 --> 00:22:10,954
It's a lot easier
than I thought it would be.

464
00:22:11,037 --> 00:22:13,248
You and me should try and pull off
a crime sometime.

465
00:22:13,331 --> 00:22:15,250
Yeah, let's rob a bank this weekend.

466
00:22:15,333 --> 00:22:17,794
I think if we go down the storm drain,
we'll hit that fence.

467
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:19,129
-Let's go.
-Okay.

468
00:22:24,885 --> 00:22:26,386
-Oh, I like this.
-[chuckles]

469
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:28,472
Feels like we're in SEAL Team 6
or something.

470
00:22:28,555 --> 00:22:30,599
I just wanna go out
and kill Osama bin Laden.

471
00:22:32,851 --> 00:22:35,396
So, uh, you see that road yet?

472
00:22:35,479 --> 00:22:36,855
You wanna call your Uber now, or...

473
00:22:36,938 --> 00:22:38,815
-No. I think we're close, though.
-Okay.

474
00:22:38,899 --> 00:22:40,817
Thanks for coming with me on this mission.
This was cool.

475
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:42,528
Yeah. It's fun, right?

476
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:44,780
-So do you think-- What?
-[shushes]

477
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:45,947
Do you hear that?

478
00:22:47,282 --> 00:22:48,659
No.

479
00:22:48,742 --> 00:22:50,285
I think somebody's nearby.

480
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:53,497
Are you fucking with me?

481
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:55,624
That's not a cool trick
to play on somebody like me.

482
00:22:55,707 --> 00:22:56,875
No. Listen.

483
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:59,753
-[leaves rustling]
-Fuck.

484
00:22:59,836 --> 00:23:01,672
-[shuddering]
-Is it coming closer?

485
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:02,964
It sounds like it's coming closer, right?

486
00:23:03,048 --> 00:23:05,050
Fuck. I think it is. This is really scary.

487
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:07,218
-Fuck.
-[officer 1] Straight ahead.

488
00:23:07,302 --> 00:23:09,763
-Oh, fuck, it's the cops. Let's run.
-Okay.

489
00:23:09,846 --> 00:23:12,265
No, no, no. Let's stay here.
We'll hide and then they'll pass.

490
00:23:12,348 --> 00:23:13,892
-Fuck that. I'm running.
-No. Mickey.

491
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:15,143
[grunting]

492
00:23:15,226 --> 00:23:18,188
Fuck. Fuck. Fuck. This is stupid!

493
00:23:19,022 --> 00:23:21,149
[Mickey] Run faster! We can lose them.

494
00:23:21,232 --> 00:23:22,275
[Gus] Fuck.

495
00:23:23,444 --> 00:23:25,737
-[Gus grunts]
-Oh, shit! Are you okay?

496
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:28,156
Yeah. I'm okay. Run!

497
00:23:28,239 --> 00:23:30,075
-Run!
-Fuck.

498
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:33,787
-[officer 1] Hey! Hey, you!
-[officer 2] There he is.

499
00:23:34,621 --> 00:23:35,622
[officer 1] Stop!

500
00:23:36,372 --> 00:23:37,916
[Gus] Whoa.

501
00:23:37,999 --> 00:23:39,585
[officer 2] Police! Stop! Stop now!

502
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:42,420
-[officer 1] Stop! Put your hands up now!
-Okay. [panting]

503
00:23:42,504 --> 00:23:44,715
-[officer 2] We found our guy.
-No. I'm not your guy.

504
00:23:44,798 --> 00:23:47,801
-[officer 1] Shut the fuck up!
-Okay. Oh, Jesus.

505
00:23:47,884 --> 00:23:50,011
-Don't move.
-I'm not. I'm just... [panting]

506
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,137
I'm sorry. I'm not trying to.

507
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:54,432
It's just when I get nervous,
my hands and my arms start to shake. Okay?

508
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:56,184
-Do you wanna get shot?
-No, no, no, no!

509
00:23:56,268 --> 00:23:59,229
I respect the police force!
I respect police. My uncle's a cop.

510
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:01,147
My uncle's a cop!
My Uncle Rodger's a cop!

511
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:04,192
-Where does he work?
-He lives in South Dakota.

512
00:24:04,275 --> 00:24:06,612
-[officer 2] You're a liar!
-I'm from the Midwest!

513
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:09,573
Hey! No.
He's not the guy you're looking for.

514
00:24:09,656 --> 00:24:11,282
It's okay. Leave him alone.

515
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:14,160
Mickey, stop.
You're not helping, okay. [grunts]

516
00:24:14,244 --> 00:24:17,413
[shrieks] Gus! Oh, my God.
Gus, are you okay?

517
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:19,583
-I'm innocent.
-He is innocent. He is.

518
00:24:19,666 --> 00:24:21,459
He was just trying
to help me get out of here.

519
00:24:21,543 --> 00:24:23,670
[groans and grunts] Fuck.

520
00:24:26,339 --> 00:24:28,884
[sighs] Oh, God damn.

521
00:24:32,012 --> 00:24:33,138
Here's your ice.

522
00:24:33,221 --> 00:24:36,182
[grunts] Thank you so much.

523
00:24:36,266 --> 00:24:38,810
I'm sorry I didn't get to the cops faster.

524
00:24:38,894 --> 00:24:41,062
Oh, it's totally cool.

525
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:46,610
-Sorry we didn't get you out of here.
-Well, sure tried.

526
00:24:46,693 --> 00:24:47,944
[chuckles]

527
00:24:48,028 --> 00:24:49,237
-Yeah.
-[sighs]

528
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,949
Yeah, we did. [grunts]

529
00:24:57,245 --> 00:24:58,454
Oh, man.

530
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:03,001
-[sighs heavily]
-I am wiped out. [sighs]

531
00:25:04,002 --> 00:25:05,754
Dude, can I just crash here?

532
00:25:09,299 --> 00:25:10,425
Yeah.

533
00:25:11,760 --> 00:25:12,928
Cool.

534
00:25:29,653 --> 00:25:32,405
If we were gonna kiss,
it would be right now.

535
00:25:34,449 --> 00:25:35,533
Yeah.

536
00:25:37,744 --> 00:25:38,745
But...

537
00:25:40,956 --> 00:25:42,248
Yeah.

538
00:25:55,553 --> 00:25:57,013
Nighty-night.

539
00:26:04,520 --> 00:26:05,939
[Mickey sighs]

540
00:26:07,857 --> 00:26:10,485
[Fleetwood Mac's "What Makes You Think
You're the One" playing]

541
00:26:10,569 --> 00:26:14,155
♪ What makes you think you're the one ♪

542
00:26:15,740 --> 00:26:18,326
♪ Who can laugh without cryin'? ♪

543
00:26:20,996 --> 00:26:24,082
♪ What makes you think you're the one ♪

544
00:26:25,750 --> 00:26:28,837
♪ Who can live without dyin'? ♪

545
00:26:29,963 --> 00:26:32,007
♪ Every little bit ♪

546
00:26:32,591 --> 00:26:34,384
♪ Is there ♪

547
00:26:34,968 --> 00:26:37,470
♪ To see ♪

548
00:26:40,015 --> 00:26:42,183
♪ Every little bit ♪

549
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:44,769
♪ Of you ♪

550
00:26:44,853 --> 00:26:47,939
♪ And me ♪

551
00:26:51,026 --> 00:26:53,111
 [vocalizing]

